	(text "GNSS / Orientation -- georeferencing the array"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25 18 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.5 2.5)
			)
		)
		(uuid "aaaa0001-0000-4000-8000-000000000001")
	)
	(text "Placement only: no wires or global labels yet.\n\nWHY THIS SHEET EXISTS. The UWB array produces position RELATIVE to the\nantenna frame -- 'tag is 6.2m out at 40deg off boresight'. To turn that into\na world coordinate a responder can act on, two things are needed, and GPS\nalone supplies only the first:\n\n  WHERE the station is   -> U9, MAX-M10S GNSS\n  WHICH WAY it is facing -> U10, LIS3MDL magnetometer\n\nPosition without heading gives a circle of possible tag locations, not a\npoint. This is the part that is easy to miss: a perfect GPS fix on its own\ndoes not georeference a bearing.\n\nU11 (LIS2DH accelerometer) is there for TILT COMPENSATION. A magnetometer\nreports heading correctly only when level; the station is carried to varying\nterrain and set down, so it will not be. Pitch and roll from U11 let\nfirmware correct the magnetic heading. U11 second job: detect that the\nstation has been knocked or moved mid-deployment, which silently invalidates\nboth the GPS fix and the heading."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.828 43.688 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "aaaa0001-0000-4000-8000-000000000002")
	)
	(text "ACCURACY, stated plainly so nobody is surprised at bring-up. Uncorrected\nGNSS is 2-5m; the UWB array targets 10-30cm. The absolute coordinate is\ntherefore 10-30x coarser than the relative fix inside the array. Relative\nprecision is untouched -- only the world-frame anchor point is coarse.\n\nThe team chose SURVEY-IN to narrow this: with the station stationary,\nfirmware averages its own fix over minutes to reach sub-metre. Note the\noperational cost, since this station is MOVED BETWEEN DEPLOYMENTS -- that\naveraging restarts at every new site, so there is a warm-up before absolute\ncoordinates are trustworthy. Relative UWB positioning is available\nimmediately and does not wait for it. Decide what the UI shows during\nwarm-up.\n\nAveraging is done in firmware on the BT840, not in the module: u-blox\n'Survey-In' proper is a feature of their timing/RTK parts, not the M10\nstandard-precision line. Averaging NMEA/UBX fixes host-side is equivalent\nfor static self-positioning and needs no more expensive part."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.066 84.074 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "aaaa0001-0000-4000-8000-000000000003")
	)
	(text "PARTS -- all three are KiCad stock symbols AND footprints, deliberately.\nThe board already carries two outstanding vendor-footprint imports (BT840,\nand DWM3001C on the tag); adding a third was not worth it. u-blox SAM-M10Q\nwith its integrated patch antenna was the alternative and would have removed\nthe GNSS antenna entirely, but KiCad has neither symbol nor footprint for\nit. MAX-M10S needs an external antenna at 1.575GHz, which is far easier\nrouting than the 6.5GHz UWB work already on this board.\n\nPIN DATA VERIFIED against the real u-blox MAX-M10S Data Sheet UBX-20035208\nR02, Table 9. KiCad's symbol matches on 17 of 18 pins. ONE DISCREPANCY:\npin 15 is 'Reserved' in R02 but named VIO_SEL in KiCad's symbol -- likely a\nlater datasheet revision. Check the current revision before connecting it;\nleave it open until then.\n\nDATASHEET CONSTRAINTS, from the same document:\n  - 'VCC and V_IO must be connected together' (absolute maximum ratings).\n    Pin 8 and pin 7 tie to the same +3V3_SYS rail.\n  - Pin 18 SAFEBOOT_N: leave OPEN.\n  - Pin 6 V_BCKP is the backup supply that preserves almanac/ephemeris for a\n    hot start. Worth feeding from +VSYS rather than the switched rail, or the\n    module cold-starts every power cycle -- which lengthens every survey-in.\n  - For an ACTIVE antenna (recommended outdoors): pin 14 VCC_RF biases it and\n    pin 13 LNA_EN switches it. Feeding DC onto the RF line needs an inductor\n    or ferrite plus a DC block; that network is NOT yet placed."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 126.746 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "aaaa0001-0000-4000-8000-000000000004")
	)
	(text "I2C: U10 and U11 share the existing bus with the MAX17048 on power_bms.\nAddresses do not collide -- MAX17048 0x36, LIS3MDL 0x1C/0x1E, LIS2DH\n0x18/0x19, the latter two selectable by their SDO strap. Pull-ups live once\non the bus, not per device; they are not placed here.\n\nGNSS talks UART to the BT840 (U9 pins 2/3), not I2C.\n\nMAGNETOMETER SITING is a layout problem, not a schematic one, and it is the\nthing most likely to ruin heading accuracy: keep U10 as far as possible from\nthe DC-DC converter, the battery, the four SMA connectors and any steel in\nthe frame. Hard-iron and soft-iron calibration in firmware corrects for\nfixed nearby metal, but not for anything that moves or switches current."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 21.844 165.1 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "aaaa0001-0000-4000-8000-000000000005")
	)
